# Security Policy

## Reporting a vulnerability

Please **do not** open a public GitHub issue for security problems.

Report privately through GitHub's private vulnerability reporting:
<https://github.com/[[ github_repo ]]/security/advisories/new>.

Include the affected version or commit, steps to reproduce, and the impact as
you understand it. We aim to acknowledge reports within 3 working days and to
fix confirmed high-severity issues within 14 days; please give us that time
before disclosing publicly.

## Secrets

If you find a credential in this repository, report it the same way. Test
fixtures intentionally use obviously fake values such as `sk_test_not-a-real-key`.

Internal handling rules: [docs/standards/SECURITY_STANDARD.md](docs/standards/SECURITY_STANDARD.md).
